-- The words a board shows for a zone, a phase or beat, a mode or a colour —
-- `wording.ts`'s refusals, `narration.ts`'s beats and `lighting.ts`'s room
-- colours, gathered as `board-words.ts`'s `BoardWords` (Stage 8, #159).
--
-- Declared rather than hand-written by the owner's decision on #131/#135
-- (20 Sep 2026): DEFINE WORDS is a declaration of its own, not a field of
-- DEFINE GAME. `of:` says which table a word belongs to; the name is the
-- zone, phase/step, mode or colour it is the word for, so `DEFINE WORDS
-- battle` is the words for `DEFINE ZONE battle` and needs no second name.
--
-- Consumed: `board-words.ts` reads every word below from the loaded
-- definition (`wordsFromRuleset`, over the generated `files.ts`), and
-- `wording.ts`, `narration.ts`, `effects.ts` and `lighting.ts` read it from
-- there (Stage 8, #159). The sentence *shapes* around the words — which branch
-- a viewer takes, the "cannot ... now" frame — stay in those files.
--
-- The last three sections are the phrases a `Requirement` and a rule in force
-- are said in: `of: verb`, `of: window` and `of: until`. Their names carry a
-- prefix because a name is unique across every `of:` (`charge` is already a
-- phase, `main` and `defense` too).

-- §3: the twelve areas the manual counts, minus the two effect-language-only
-- routes (`under`, `play`) `zones.rules` also declares — a program needs to
-- name them, but a board never shows them as a place a card sits, so
-- `board-words.ts`'s own tables carry no entry for either and neither does
-- this file. Order follows `zones.rules`.
DEFINE WORDS deck
  of: zone
  you: "your deck"
  text: "the deck"

DEFINE WORDS hand
  of: zone
  you: "your hand"
  text: "hand"

DEFINE WORDS drop
  of: zone
  you: "your Drop Area"
  text: "the Drop"

DEFINE WORDS leader
  of: zone
  you: "the Leader Area"
  text: "the Leader Area"

DEFINE WORDS battle
  of: zone
  you: "your Battle Area"
  text: "the Battle Area"

DEFINE WORDS combo
  of: zone
  you: "your Combo Area"
  text: "the Combo Area"

DEFINE WORDS energy
  of: zone
  you: "your Energy Area"
  text: "the Energy Area"

DEFINE WORDS life
  of: zone
  you: "your Life Area"
  text: "life"

DEFINE WORDS warp
  of: zone
  you: "your Warp"
  text: "the Warp"

DEFINE WORDS unison
  of: zone
  you: "the Unison Area"
  text: "the Unison Area"

DEFINE WORDS zDeck
  of: zone
  you: "your Z-Deck"
  text: "the Z-Deck"

DEFINE WORDS zEnergy
  of: zone
  you: "your Z-Energy Area"
  text: "Z-Energy"

DEFINE WORDS removed
  of: zone
  you: "out of the game"
  text: "out of the game"

-- §6, §7: the six turn phases and the two a turn is not made of (`setup`,
-- `over`), as `narration.ts`'s beat stream names them, plus the five battle
-- sub-flow steps a "phase" beat also narrates (`declared`..`battleEnd`,
-- `board-words.ts`'s own `PHASE_DECLARATION` maps each to `game.rules`'s
-- `mainEnd` or to `battle.rules`'s own step). Order follows `PHASE` there.
DEFINE WORDS charge
  of: phase
  text: "Charge Phase"

DEFINE WORDS main
  of: phase
  text: "Main Phase"

DEFINE WORDS mainEnd
  of: phase
  text: "Main Phase ends"

DEFINE WORDS end
  of: phase
  text: "End Phase"

DEFINE WORDS declared
  of: phase
  text: "Attack declared"

DEFINE WORDS offense
  of: phase
  text: "Offense Step"

DEFINE WORDS defense
  of: phase
  text: "Defense Step"

DEFINE WORDS damage
  of: phase
  text: "Damage Step"

DEFINE WORDS battleEnd
  of: phase
  text: "The battle ends"

DEFINE WORDS setup
  of: phase
  text: "Setting up"

DEFINE WORDS over
  of: phase
  text: "The game is over"

-- §1-10: the only two tokens `zones.rules` declares for a zone's `modes:`.
DEFINE WORDS active
  of: mode
  text: "Active Mode"

DEFINE WORDS rest
  of: mode
  text: "Rest Mode"

-- §1-2-3: the seven colours `attributes.rules`' own `colors` attribute may
-- hold. `room: true` marks the five a Leader can be, and so a room can be lit
-- for (`lighting.ts`'s `LEADER_COLOURS`) — White and Colorless light no room
-- of their own (`colourOf`'s own fallback to Black).
DEFINE WORDS Red
  of: color
  room: true
  text: "Red"

DEFINE WORDS Blue
  of: color
  room: true
  text: "Blue"

DEFINE WORDS Green
  of: color
  room: true
  text: "Green"

DEFINE WORDS Yellow
  of: color
  room: true
  text: "Yellow"

DEFINE WORDS Black
  of: color
  room: true
  text: "Black"

DEFINE WORDS White
  of: color
  text: "White"

DEFINE WORDS Colorless
  of: color
  text: "Colorless"

-- `wording.ts`'s verb in "X cannot <verb> now", one per action a client can
-- ask for. An action with no word here is said "do that" (the shape's own
-- default).
DEFINE WORDS verbAttack
  of: verb
  text: "attack"

DEFINE WORDS verbCombo
  of: verb
  text: "combo"

DEFINE WORDS verbPlay
  of: verb
  text: "be played"

DEFINE WORDS verbPlayUnison
  of: verb
  text: "be played"

DEFINE WORDS verbPlayZ
  of: verb
  text: "be played"

DEFINE WORDS verbActivate
  of: verb
  text: "use its skill"

DEFINE WORDS verbCharge
  of: verb
  text: "be charged"

DEFINE WORDS verbCounter
  of: verb
  text: "counter"

DEFINE WORDS verbBlock
  of: verb
  text: "block"

DEFINE WORDS verbChoose
  of: verb
  text: "be chosen"

-- `wording.ts`'s remedy for a timing refusal: when the action is allowed. A
-- window with no word here is said "Only in the <window>." by the shape.
DEFINE WORDS windowMain
  of: window
  text: "Only in your Main Phase."

DEFINE WORDS windowBattle
  of: window
  text: "Only during a battle."

DEFINE WORDS windowDefense
  of: window
  text: "Only in the Defense Step of your opponent's turn."

DEFINE WORDS windowNextTurn
  of: window
  text: "No attacks on the first turn — from your next turn on."

-- `effects.ts`'s `untilWords`: how long a rule in force holds, one per
-- duration. `{them}` is the other player's name and `{source}` the card
-- holding a rule up. Where the phrase depends on whose turn ends it, `you:`
-- is the one that names the viewer and `text:` the one that names the other
-- player; `bare:` is `text:` with no `{source}` to fill.
DEFINE WORDS untilTurn
  of: until
  text: "until the end of the turn"

DEFINE WORDS untilBattle
  of: until
  text: "for the battle"

DEFINE WORDS untilNextTurn
  of: until
  you: "until the start of your next turn"
  text: "until the start of {them}'s next turn"

DEFINE WORDS untilOpponentTurn
  of: until
  you: "until the start of your next turn"
  text: "until the start of {them}'s next turn"

DEFINE WORDS untilAfterNextCharge
  of: until
  text: "through the next Charge Phase"

DEFINE WORDS untilGame
  of: until
  text: "for the rest of the game"

DEFINE WORDS untilPermanent
  of: until
  text: "while {source} is in play"
  bare: "while its card is in play"
